PASS  BOT-SEC-05       functions/chat/** reads no NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable
PASS  BOT-IDX-01       the retrieval index exists and is internally consistent
PASS  BOT-IDX-02       the index is built from the same dataset version the site renders (R-108)
PASS  BOT-IDX-03       every chunk carries a provenance record with a real retrievedAt
PASS  BOT-IDX-04       chunk text is one atomic claim: 40 to 320 characters
PASS  BOT-IDX-05       R-111: every numeral in a chunk is a numeral the chunk actually contains
PASS  BOT-IDX-06       df and postings agree, term for term
PASS  BOT-IDX-07       indexHash is the canonical hash of the chunks it ships
PASS  BOT-IDX-08       R-69: every chunk deep-links somewhere real, and channel chunks invent no timestamp
PASS  BOT-IDX-09       R-175: a not-observable field is a sourced statement of absence, never a zero
PASS  BOT-IDX-10       the entity allow-list is generated from the corpus, never hand-added
PASS  BOT-IDX-11       the alias table is small, readable, and never manufactures a hit
PASS  BOT-INDEX-02     TC-BOT-INDEX-02: the index ships zero bytes to the browser
PASS  BOT-RL-01        the limiter enforces the four §6.1 windows and never writes a raw IP
PASS  BOT-COLOPHON-01  R-183: the counter and the sentence that discloses it ship together
PASS  BOT-PKG-01       chat:index, chat:calibrate and chat:probe exist and the build runs the index
PASS  BOT-PKG-02       the builder and the two probes exist on disk

